[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Process Managers in Node.js: PM2 and Nodemon"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Node.js applications often require continuous uptime and efficient management. Process managers like PM2 and Nodemon provide solutions for automatically restarting applications after crashes, facilitating zero-downtime deployments, and monitoring application performance. This tutorial explores PM2 and Nodemon, highlighting their features and usage."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Nodemon: Automatic Restart on File Changes"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Nodemon is a utility that monitors for any changes in your Node.js application and automatically restarts the server. It's primarily used during development to streamline the development workflow."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automatic Restart: Restarts the Node.js application whenever file changes are detected."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Simple Configuration: Easy to set up and use with minimal configuration."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"# Installation
npm install -g nodemon"},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"# Usage
nodemon your-node-app.js"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Nodemon can be configured using a 'nodemon.json' file in the root directory of your project. This file allows you to specify files to ignore, extensions to watch, and other options."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"{ 
  "ignore": ["node_modules/*", "test/*"],
  "ext": "js json"
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"PM2: Production Process Manager"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"PM2 is a production process manager for Node.js applications with a built-in load balancer. It allows you to keep applications alive forever, reload them without downtime, and facilitate common system admin tasks."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automatic Restart: Restarts applications automatically after crashes or unexpected exits."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Load Balancing: Built-in load balancer to distribute traffic across multiple instances of your application."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Monitoring: Provides real-time monitoring of CPU usage, memory usage, and other metrics."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Log Management: Centralized log management for easy debugging and troubleshooting."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Startup Script Generation: Generates startup scripts to automatically start applications on system boot."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"# Installation
npm install -g pm2"},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"# Start an application
pm2 start your-node-app.js --name "MyApp""},{"order":20,"type":"code","text":"# List running processes
pm2 list"},{"order":21,"type":"code","text":"# Stop an application
pm2 stop MyApp"},{"order":22,"type":"code","text":"# Restart an application
pm2 restart MyApp"},{"order":23,"type":"code","text":"# Delete an application
pm2 delete MyApp"},{"order":24,"type":"code","text":"# Monitor application logs
pm2 logs MyApp"},{"order":25,"type":"code","text":"# Enable startup script generation
pm2 startup"},{"order":26,"type":"paragraph","text":"PM2 can also be configured using a 'ecosystem.config.js' file. This file allows you to define multiple applications, specify environment variables, and configure deployment options."},{"order":27,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  apps : [{
    name   : "MyApp",
    script : 'your-node-app.js',
    instances : "max",
    autorestart : true,
    watch : false,
    max_memory_restart : '1G',
    env : {
      NODE_ENV: "development"
    },
    env_production : {
      NODE_ENV: "production"
    }
  }]
};"},{"order":28,"type":"code","text":"# Start applications defined in ecosystem.config.js
pm2 start ecosystem.config.js"},{"order":29,"type":"subheading","text":"Choosing Between Nodemon and PM2"},{"order":30,"type":"paragraph","text":"Nodemon is best suited for development environments where automatic restarts on file changes are beneficial. PM2 is designed for production environments where high availability, load balancing, and monitoring are crucial."},{"order":31,"type":"paragraph","text":"In summary, use Nodemon during development to speed up the development process, and use PM2 in production to ensure your Node.js application runs reliably and efficiently."}]
